      "description": "INDIGO Park Canada Inc. is a Montreal-based parking, mobility and EV-services operator active across Canada. Founded in Quebec City in 1988, the company remained a distinct legal and operating business after LAZ Parking completed a 60% acquisition on June 30, 2025; INDIGO Group retained 40%. INDIGO Group's FY2025 accounts state that LAZ committed under the sale agreement to acquire the remaining 40% in 2029, but the exact future closing date and valuation are not yet publicly fixed. The current company site reports more than 340,000 parking stalls across 95 cities and nearly 450,000 active app users. Argo Infrastructure Partners' directly evidenced manager-level investment is LAZ, not INDIGO Park Canada. INDIGO Park Canada is therefore archived from the standalone manager-level PortCo census as an active LAZ subsidiary, without a legal merge, redirect or Argo exit; the contractual 2029 ownership change remains pending.",
